INT. PLANETARIUM DOME - NIGHT

Stars wheel overhead on a painted ceiling. Reclining seats ring a projector like a metal spider.

ZELDA, thirties, in a black bodysuit, clips a wire. MOE, fifties, her partner, kneels at the projector. KIRSTEN, forties, the planetarium director, bound to a seat with tape. BAXTER, twenties, a guard, lies unconscious. YUSUF, thirties, watches the door.

A STRANGER, forties, in a long coat, steps out of the dark aisle.

Zelda turns. Kirsten wriggles. Moe freezes. He raises a wrench. She lowers her wire cutters.

STRANGER
Evening. I'm told the Orion diamond is on display tonight.

ZELDA
It isn't.

STRANGER
It's under the projector.

Yusuf slides toward the stranger. He grabs his collar. The stranger doesn't flinch.

STRANGER (CONT'D)
My name is Lucian. I'm the buyer.

YUSUF
The buyer isn't due until Friday.

LUCIAN
I'm early. She knows.

He nods at Kirsten. She nods back. Zelda stares at her. She stares at Zelda.

ZELDA
You sold us out.

KIRSTEN
I sold you a ceiling, dear.

Moe drops the wrench. The stars blink out.
